From 6cf88c1271feb9043cea99fd9e1c20e36259a44d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Report what targeting buys, how the numbers depend on the
 reference, and the new-build gap

Exposure counts only degrees above the typical block (45.7 C), so measures on
blocks below it cannot change it. New, reproducible outputs make that explicit
(the pre-pitch review's section 3 and 4 numbers, recomputed by the pipeline):

- interventions.targeting_comparison: cool roofs + pocket parks on every block,
  the riskiest third and only the 106 blocks above the reference all give -74%
  (126 / 44 / 23 ha); a random third gives -25% (90% of draws -19% to -31%);
  the most-populated third -0.5%.
- interventions.heat_line_sensitivity: every result at the urban quartiles
  44.5 / 45.7 / 47.0 C; the targeted plan holds at -65% to -84%.
- interventions.resident_weighted_cooling: a threshold-free ranking (cool roofs
  -0.72 C per resident, pocket parks -0.55, pavements -0.37, trees -0.13).
- targeted_plan also reports residents of treated blocks above the reference
  (10,487 of 22,588); README and notebook 00 say 'treated', not 'cooled'.
- growth.controlled_new_build_gap: new blocks are +0.95 C raw but +0.22 C after
  allowing for cover, sand and vegetation.
- run_example rounds result floats to 9 significant digits, so re-runs give
  byte-identical results/*.json (BLAS noise no longer dirties git).
- README: the targeting line, the new results rows, test count 27, and two
  limits (pocket parks likely overstated about 2x; irrigation not modelled).
- Notebook 00 re-executed from a clean kernel with the new cells.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
