+- Targeted plan (cool roofs + pocket parks on the riskiest third, 192 blocks): 6,460 → 1,686 person·°C (**-74%**), 22,588 residents in treated blocks (10,487 of them in blocks above the typical block).
+
+## Does choosing the blocks matter? (cool roofs + pocket parks)
+Exposure counts only degrees above the typical block, so blocks below it cannot change it: targeting saves area rather than adding cuts.
+
+| Where | Blocks | Area coated or greened | Exposure change |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Every block | 576 | 126 ha | -74% |
+| Riskiest third | 192 | 44 ha | -74% |
+| Only blocks above the typical block | 106 | 23 ha | -74% |
+| A random third (median of draws) | 192 | 42 ha | -25% |
+| The most-populated third | 192 | 47 ha | -0.5% |
+- Random thirds: 90% of 500 draws between -19% and -31%.
+
+## How much the percentages depend on the reference temperature
+| Reference (urban quartiles) | cool roofs | street trees | cool pavements | pocket parks | targeted plan |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 44.5 °C | -49% | -19% | -43% | -54% | -65% |
+| 45.7 °C | -41% | -24% | -52% | -60% | -74% |
+| 47.0 °C | -28% | -44% | -71% | -82% | -84% |
+- With no reference at all, the average surface change per resident (one measure everywhere): cool roofs -0.72 °C, pocket parks -0.55 °C, cool pavements -0.37 °C, street trees -0.13 °C.
 
